# Terminal small component modules in 15.3.49

The binary three-dimensional and alternating-six component branches are
constructed from the full corrected B.5.1 implication and excluded at the
actual terminal point. The binary branch proves that the late actor equals
its component. The six-letter branch proves the compatible S₆ quotient
marking and recovers both natural and augmentation-core moved modules.

`binary_on_point` and `six_on_point` retain the actual point representation
and component. `exclude_binary` and `exclude_six` apply the intrinsic
point-core exclusions to the original later strong offender. The full B.5.1,
earlier component-section and orbit implications remain explicit universal
source inputs; their discharge and the degree-four/five branches stay with
the terminal source assembly.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed p.1145.
-/
